        "finalMessage": "I fixed both issues in `collapsible.tsx`, but I couldn't confirm it with the linter: running `npx ultracite check` needs approval, which this session doesn't have.\n\n**What changed:** the clickable header `<div>` is now a `<button type=\"button\">` with `aria-expanded={open}`. That clears both errors:\n- **no-static-element-interactions:** the click handler is now on a real interactive element.\n- **click-events-have-key-events:** a native button already responds to Enter and Space and can be focused with Tab, so it doesn't need a separate key handler.\n\nI first tried keeping the `div` and adding `role=\"button\"`, `tabIndex`, and a key handler. I dropped that because Ultracite's React preset also turns on `jsx-a11y/prefer-tag-over-role`, which would have flagged the `div` as a new error.\n\n**Keeping the look the same:** I added inline styles that undo the browser's default button styling: no background, border, padding or margin, and inherited `font`, `color` and `textAlign`. I also added `width: \"100%\"`, because a button doesn't stretch to full width the way a `div` does. Clicking still calls `openTrigger` exactly as before, and `className` is still applied.\n\n**One thing for you to decide:** in Excalidraw, the `label` passed in is an `<h3>`. Strictly, HTML doesn't allow a heading inside a `<button>`. Browsers display it fine, but screen readers announce it as part of the button, not as a heading (the `role=\"button\"` version would have had the same problem). The standard pattern is `<h3><button>…</button></h3>`, but that means changing the callers in `Stats/index.tsx`, which is outside this one-file task.",
        "styleMentions": [
          "**Keeping the look the same:** I added inline styles that undo the browser's default button styling: no background, border, padding or margin, and inherited `font`, `color` and `textAlign`.",
          "Clicking still calls `openTrigger` exactly as before, and `className` is still applied."
